<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Poland</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Polish</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Poland is a country in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. United with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, it formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> from 1569, one of the largest states in Europe, until its partition by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> in the late eighteenth century. It was restored as an independent state in 1918 from territories of the Russian, German and Austro-Hungarian empires.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/poland.jpg" alt="Poland" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: See below. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Poland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
